WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:06.420
Speaker 1: There is a stunning new report
out of Politico that officials in Palm Beach,

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:12.320
Florida, are actively contingency planning
for a possible indictment of former President

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:19.110
Donald Trump by Manhattan District Attorney
Cy Vance Jr., which could happen while Donald

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:22.040
Trump is at his Florida club, Mar a Lago.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:27.800
That this is even something being gamed out
by Palm Beach officials is stunning.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:32.040
The sources here are two high ranking county
officials from Palm Beach involved in these

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.410
planning sessions.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:37.649
The real legal question is that of extradition
from Florida to New York in the event of a

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:39.550
New York indictment of Trump.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:44.950
Now, what's ironic or tragic or I don't know
what to call it, is that because of an obscure

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:49.920
Florida statute about interstate extradition,
it would basically come down to the Florida

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:55.670
governor, who currently is the pro Trump Republican
Governor Ron DeSantis, who could ultimately

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:01.870
decide to intervene and do an investigation
of his own to determine whether the indicted

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.780
person should be extradited to another state.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.530
Joe Abruzzo, clerk of the Circuit Court of
Palm Beach.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:12.700
And he says, quote, The statute leaves room
for interpretation that the governor has the

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:17.680
power to order a review and potentially not
comply with the extradition notice.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:23.390
Now, on the other hand, Trump is currently
moving from Mar a Lago in Florida to his Bedminster,

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.600
New Jersey, estate for the summer.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:30.180
If a New York City indictment came down with
Trump and Jersey, it's a different ballgame.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.340
There's also a statute there allowing the
governor to intervene.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:38.600
But the governor in New Jersey is Democrat
Phil Murphy, not a Trump sycophant brownnoser

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.659
would likely just not get involved at all.

00:01:40.659 --> 00:01:45.149
And if Trump were in New Jersey at the time
of the indictment, Trump likely would be extradited

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:46.270
to New York.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:48.259
So there's multiple layers here to consider.

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:52.990
First of all, imagine a former president getting
indicted period would be one of the biggest

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:56.159
news stories in American political history,
period.

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:01.119
Second, imagine if former President Trump
is indicted and he's in Florida and Florida

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:04.210
Governor Ron DeSantis refuses to extradite
Trump.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:08.300
Consider what that would mean in terms of
the legal insanity of a governor protecting

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.980
a former president from extradition on an
indictment and that Trump would essentially

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:18.019
become a fugitive in his own country, at least
to his native New York, and likely wouldn't

00:02:18.019 --> 00:02:20.730
be able to travel to New York on the risk
of arrest.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:27.420
Now, I think that while de Santos would plot
plausibly intervene, there are plenty of Republican

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.640
officials who love the idea of Trump and an
indictment as a way to finally get Trump out

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:37.019
of the way and try to commandeer Trump's very
constituents for themselves.

00:02:37.019 --> 00:02:42.420
These would be the Republicans who publicly
still stand by Trump, but probably privately

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.540
think he's an idiot and bad for the Republican
Party.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.120
Could Ron DeSantis even try to intervene?

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:52.299
But in exchange for something, imagine dissent
is going to Trump and saying I'll intervene

00:02:52.299 --> 00:02:55.330
to stop the extradition, but then you owe
me.

00:02:55.330 --> 00:03:00.810
And what I want is for you not to run in 2024
and to endorse me for president in twenty

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.140
twenty four, I don't know.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:07.970
But Trump being stuck in Florida without being
able to leave is already pretty rich.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:12.030
Having to endorse the guy that saves him would
be a just delightful possibility.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:14.610
Now, do I think any of this will happen?

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:15.610
Very unlikely.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:19.550
I know we've all thought about that perp walk,
that potential moment where Donald Trump is

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.659
handcuffed and walked in front of the cameras.

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:25.099
But that is so far from a real possibility.

00:03:25.099 --> 00:03:27.769
Even if Trump were indicted, he wouldn't be
perp walked.

00:03:27.769 --> 00:03:29.040
It would all be very quiet.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.200
And quite frankly, I think it's all very far
fetched.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:37.599
But the fact that it's potentially real enough
that officials around the country are thinking

00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:41.319
about if Trump is indicted, how do we handle
it?

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:43.350
That's already historic.

